.TH UDB 1 "November 2026" "udb 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
udb \- initialize an Ubuntu development environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B udb
.RB [ \-p " | " \-w ]
.RB [ \-c ]
.RB [ \-t " TENANT" ]
.RB [ \-\-skip-login ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
udb initializes an Ubuntu 22.04, 24.04, or 26.04 development environment
on amd64 or arm64, either standalone with systemd or on WSL2.
Run it as an ordinary user with sudo access, not as root or through sh.
.PP
Installing the package only installs the command and documentation.
Initialization happens only when the user explicitly runs udb.
Existing compatible installations and user-owned configuration are preserved.
Failures are reported per task; independent tasks continue.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-personal
Use the personal profile, including WorkIQ installation and login.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-work
Use the work profile (the default).
Skip WorkIQ unless an explicit tenant is supplied.
Personal and work profiles are mutually exclusive.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-china-mirror
Select the supported China download and package mirrors.
.TP
.BR \-pc ", " \-wc
Combine the corresponding profile with China mirror mode.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tenant " TENANT"
Explicitly select the Azure tenant for login.
Neither profile supplies a default tenant.
.TP
.B \-\-skip-login
Skip GitHub, Azure, Copilot, and WorkIQ login.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display the complete operational help without initializing the machine.
.SH SIDE EFFECTS
Explicit initialization upgrades apt packages and may install third-party
tools, change the login shell, and configure Docker.
Docker group membership grants root-equivalent access.
On WSL, initialization may configure passwordless sudo.
Copilot shortcuts use the upstream yolo option.
When WorkIQ login is selected, its EULA is accepted if not already recorded.
Read the complete help before proceeding on a machine you control.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means all requested tasks completed or were explicitly skipped.
Nonzero means an invalid invocation, interrupted execution, or failed or
blocked tasks. Consult the printed per-task logs and recovery commands.
